# Round qt-glue: ik's CPU node dumps of the istaglue fixture variant (/models/fixture-variants/istaglue/v41), the four V4.1
# fixture sets (step4, d1n, d1, d2 every-node), each one `BLOOMERY_TIER=fixture BLOOMERY_FIXTURE_VARIANT=istaglue just
# dump-ref-fixture deepseek41 <set>-every-node` under this card, one lease each. Nothing is timed.
# Minutes [derived]: the base fixture's V4.1 dumps were 0.05-0.3 min each (docs/cards/fxoracle-dump.card, fxprobe's measured
# walls, V4.1 1.4 s) plus 3-15 s a lease take; four takes: 1-5 min.
kind: exclusive
reason: dump_ref runs ik on 32 CPU threads and pages the variant file in, so it holds the lease; why now: gate-gpu-ds41-step
  on the istaglue variant has no oracle sets until ik has dumped the variant, and the Q5_K embedding and IQ4_NL engram
  decodes are otherwise held only to our own host decode
minutes: 1..5
